WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.920
From battling alongside Xena&nbsp;
to painting with beeswax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.569
here's what the actor who played&nbsp;
Gabrielle has been up to lately.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.520
Just as "Xena: Warrior Princess" helped put&nbsp;
Renée O'Connor on the map, it also kick-started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:19.200
her love for directing. The actor got the&nbsp;
opportunity to direct the "Xena" Season 4 finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.880
and she later helmed an episode in Season 6.&nbsp;
After her time on "Xena: Warrior Princess,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.760
O'Connor founded ROC Productions and&nbsp;
went on to direct award-winning shorts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.320
as well as some lesser-known full-length films.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.080
She co-directed "Diamonds and Guns"&nbsp;
as her first feature film directing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.925
credit while starring in the project&nbsp;
and acting as executive producer.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.040
"Do you recognize me?"

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.520
According to O'Connor, the move from&nbsp;
acting on screen in a TV show for six years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.120
to the production side of things&nbsp;
came with a steep learning curve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.360
She produced a number of shorts, including&nbsp;
"Words Unspoken," which won her awards for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.920
Best Short Film and Best Actress at the&nbsp;
West Hollywood International Film Festival.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.880
When asked what inspired her to direct&nbsp;
"Words Unspoken," O'Connor told Film Nut:

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.000
"I wanted to direct something where I didn't have&nbsp;
to compromise to a studio, such as to a television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.560
show. I could really just be authentic&nbsp;
in my own voice and in my own visions."

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.280
It seems like she ran with that wish, as O'Connor&nbsp;
went on to direct her second feature film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.640
"Broken Things," a few years later in 2015.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:27.120
In 2017, "Watch the Sky'' was released. O'Connor&nbsp;
played a dual role in the family sci-fi film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.895
appearing on screen while also&nbsp;
acting as executive producer.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.920
Somewhere between beasting out as Gabrielle&nbsp;
on "Xena: Warrior Princess" and diving into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.440
different roles on movie sets, Renée O'Connor&nbsp;
tackled the biggest job of all: creating and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:47.040
raising a family. She married her first husband,&nbsp;
Steve Muir, while still playing Gabrielle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.320
and she gave birth to their first child,&nbsp;
Miles, shortly after the series ended in 2001.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.440
The transition to motherhood wasn't an easy&nbsp;
one. In an interview with Camera Conversations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.800
O'Connor explained:

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.080
"I had been busy for so many years ... for&nbsp;
six years, working 80 to 90 hours a week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.840
and then suddenly that was all gone&nbsp;
and it was just a baby and myself."

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.160
After her marriage to Muir&nbsp;
ended, O'Connor married Jed Sura,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.360
who has partnered with her on many projects.&nbsp;
The two share a daughter: Iris Sura O'Connor.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.360
Both of her children inherited the acting&nbsp;
bug, performing in her production "Watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:27.520
the Sky" alongside their mom. Iris also&nbsp;
had a role in ROC Productions' "Infinity,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.421
and Miles was in an episode of&nbsp;
the show "My Life is Murder."

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.800
After the finale of "Xena: Warrior Princess,"&nbsp;
Renée O'Connor acted in a number of low budget&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.560
B-movies and monster films. One such flick was&nbsp;
"Alien Apocalypse," in which she starred opposite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.520
horror and B-movie legend Bruce Campbell.&nbsp;
The film is exactly what it sounds like:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.200
An apocalypse movie that takes place&nbsp;
after aliens have taken over Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.160
The two stars shared a kiss in the film,&nbsp;
which Campbell deemed "Sa-weet!" in a tweet.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.840
"Isn't she something?"

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.560
Unsurprisingly, fans were graced with this&nbsp;
union of cult icons because the two have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:08.400
solid connection with Mr. Sam Raimi, executive&nbsp;
producer of "Hercules: The Legendary Journeys"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.320
and "Xena: Warrior Princess." And it's&nbsp;
thanks to Campbell’s long professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.400
relationship with Raimi that he landed the&nbsp;
recurring role of Autolycus in both series.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.235
"Well, let's hope he's at least as debonair&nbsp;
and charming as I am or no one will be fooled."

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.480
Renée O'Connor also branched&nbsp;
out into live theater.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.520
She took on the role of Lady Macbeth in 2002,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:33.120
but, according to Broadway World, she didn't fully&nbsp;
get into a theater career until 15 years later.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.600
In addition to playing Lady Macbeth more&nbsp;
than once, O'Connor has played the Nurse in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:42.560
a production of "Romeo and Juliet," in which&nbsp;
her son Miles Muir held the role of Romeo.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.400
Though she's had roles in multiple&nbsp;
Shakespearean plays and classics like "Annie,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:52.480
"Mary Poppins," and "The Wizard of Oz," she's&nbsp;
also starred in more modern dramas. In 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.560
O'Connor joined the cast of "Dinner with&nbsp;
Friends" at Little Fish Theatre. She has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.840
played a number of roles at the venue, including&nbsp;
the lead in Steven Dietz's "On Clover Road."

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.160
Just like her Hollywood career, O'Connor&nbsp;
expanded her live theater one by sitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.680
in the director's chair. She helmed&nbsp;
a production of "Romeo and Juliet,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.361
sharing the experience with fans in an&nbsp;
Instagram post of herself directing onstage.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.480
Next, Renée O'Connor founded her&nbsp;
own nonprofit theater company:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.240
House of Bards, located in San Pedro. In addition&nbsp;
to producing, she typically takes a dual role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.800
either acting in or directing the productions.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.280
According to Broadway World, House of Bards&nbsp;
Theatre Company's first production was "Macbeth"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:37.760
in 2019, starring O'Connor and her husband Jed&nbsp;
Sura as the leads. Sura co-founded the theater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.240
company with O'Connor and has been partnering&nbsp;
on projects since well before its conception.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.840
House of Bards presented its second&nbsp;
play with "Romeo and Juliet" — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.967
same production O'Connor directed,&nbsp;
which had its last show in May of 2022.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:56.160
Renée O'Connor’s artistic ability goes beyond&nbsp;
the screen and stage. During the lockdown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.800
she updated her official website with an art page&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:03.280
full of paintings she made. She would use&nbsp;
a mixture of beeswax and resin crystals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.080
combined with pigments to create layers of&nbsp;
translucent colors that form an overall image.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.680
This wasn't the first time O'Connor&nbsp;
has demonstrated her love of painting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.280
In an interview with Hobo Trash Can,&nbsp;
she revealed that she used the money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:19.360
she earned from selling paintings to&nbsp;
help fund her first production venture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:24.160
"Diamonds and Guns." That film came out in&nbsp;
2008, so it's clear that painting has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.895
another creative outlet for the former "Xena:&nbsp;
Warrior Princess" star for quite some time.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:34.160
If you assumed that spending six years opposite&nbsp;
each other on a world-renowned hit TV series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.640
would make Renée O'Connor and Lucy Lawless&nbsp;
pretty tight, you aren't wrong. While the "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:42.320
Warrior Princess" stars can go years&nbsp;
at a time without seeing each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.520
they have nonetheless stayed good&nbsp;
friends following the series.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:49.120
When asked about their relationship&nbsp;
in an interview with the Toronto Star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.960
Lawless revealed that, very much like&nbsp;
their "Xena: Warrior Princess" roles:

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.200
"It’s a sisterhood. It’s beyond&nbsp;
friends, forged in the heat of battle."

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:01.200
"Xena: Warrior Princess" was filmed in&nbsp;
New Zealand — Lawless' home country and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.480
where she still resides. O'Connor, on the other&nbsp;
hand, is an American who relocated to transform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.120
into Gabrielle for the series. She returned to&nbsp;
the States after the show ended, which put quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:15.695
the physical distance between the two stars,&nbsp;
but they've always found ways to reconnect.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:21.120
Renée O'Connor traveled to New Zealand during the&nbsp;
lockdown to reunite with her former co-star when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:27.680
she accepted a one-off role in Lawless' Acorn&nbsp;
TV mystery series "My Life Is Murder." In 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:32.720
O'Connor appeared in an episode as the wife&nbsp;
of a health guru who ends up dead. The "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.280
Warrior Princess" alums found themselves&nbsp;
going head to head in "My Life is Murder"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:41.920
rather than fighting together like the good old&nbsp;
days — a refreshing change for the two friends.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.440
According to an interview the reunited&nbsp;
stars gave to Entertainment Weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:49.040
it had been a while since they had seen&nbsp;
each other. This — combined with O'Connor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:54.160
wearing a mask — made it so Lawless didn't even&nbsp;
recognize her at first. Despite that and the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:59.680
that O'Connor hadn't been on a TV set in quite&nbsp;
some time, the onscreen reunion was easygoing.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.000
"It just felt like walking into Lucy's living room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.480
and having friends over. It was so charming&nbsp;
and loving. And it was like that all the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:10.789
to the very end. I actually had a little&nbsp;
withdrawal when I finished filming."

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.800
"My Life Is Murder" isn't the only recent&nbsp;
collaboration between the former "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:20.320
Warrior Princess" stars. Prior to their reunion&nbsp;
on Lucy Lawless' show, the two actors reunited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:26.800
remotely for their series' 25th anniversary.&nbsp;
Syfy Fangrrls put together a five-episode podcast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:31.280
that was a total blast from the past for&nbsp;
both fans and those involved in "Xena."

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.000
Just as stars like Bruce Campbell and Ted Raimi&nbsp;
returned to talk about their time on the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.400
O'Connor and Lawless have their own episode&nbsp;
together. In Episode 2 of the "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.200
Warrior Princess" 25th Anniversary Podcast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:48.400
the two reminisce about all the less-than-ideal&nbsp;
conditions of filming the series in New Zealand.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.680
Lucy Lawless recounts the time rats were dumped on&nbsp;
her while filming an uncomfortable scene, saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:58.800
she had them up her Xena skirt and spiders in her&nbsp;
mouth. While that might sound like a horrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:04.167
day, looking back on the situation together seems&nbsp;
like it was a lot more fun for the co-stars.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.120
Renée O'Connor and Lucy Lawless seem to have gone&nbsp;
through the wringer when they were filming "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:14.400
Warrior Princess," but you wouldn't expect&nbsp;
anything less from two killer Amazonian warriors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.960
As it turns out, the stars also became&nbsp;
lesbian icons after they appeared as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:24.800
Xena and Gabrielle. O'Connor was voted&nbsp;
LesbiaNation's Most Loved Woman in 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:29.840
beating out Lawless, who still came in&nbsp;
second. In 2007, their places swapped.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.840
The series hints at a romantic&nbsp;
relationship between Xena and Gabrielle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:38.800
even though it never became canon that the two&nbsp;
were together. However, after the series ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:44.800
Lawless made the truth about the relationship&nbsp;
clear, telling SiriusXM in 2010 that,

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.045
"Xena and Gabrielle were a couple."

00:08:48.446 --> 00:08:50.560
“I love you Xena.”

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:53.920
When speaking to Page Six about&nbsp;
the lesbian undertones of "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.920
Warrior Princess," O'Connor said she&nbsp;
felt that if the show were on today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.440
the characters would have no need&nbsp;
to only hint at their relationship.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.960
“Are you in love with Gabrielle?”

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.640
Although it was only implied, it was still&nbsp;
groundbreaking for the time — something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:14.887
the LGBTQ community could latch onto as a&nbsp;
kind of representation in mainstream media.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:19.440
Although Gabrielle and Xena's relationship was&nbsp;
a hot topic back when the show was on the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:24.480
the characters are still very much beloved by&nbsp;
their loyal fanbase. O'Connor and Lawless have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.800
both attended their fair share of conventions&nbsp;
for "Xena: Warrior Princess" over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.960
giving the former co-stars opportunities&nbsp;
to catch up with fans and each other.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:36.880
Fan events and conventions take O'Connor&nbsp;
and Lawless all over the map, but for two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:41.360
people who live thousands of miles away from each&nbsp;
other, they're pretty much the perfect excuse to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:46.400
be in the same city. During multi-day events,&nbsp;
the two actors tend to appear on the same day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:52.240
to greet fans and answer questions. This was&nbsp;
exemplified by Creation Entertainment's 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:56.800
Salute to Xena event, which celebrated&nbsp;
the series' quarter-century milestone.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.160
Both actors enjoy interacting with&nbsp;
the convention crowds. During the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:06.720
2018 Fan Expo Canada in Toronto, Lawless thrilled&nbsp;
attendees by calling O'Connor her "screen wife."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:12.679
All these years post-"Xena," the two stars still&nbsp;
have a great time together — and with their fans.

